# Consult Jev (Agent Core) at the start of every session

**Owner instruction (2026-10-16):** Jev must be invoked every session. This rule is how.

## What to do

Once, at the beginning of each session — before planning or editing:

```powershell
cd G:\ProjectAI\rae-attendance-system-v2
. .\agent\scripts\use-live-credentials.ps1   # DPAPI store -> this shell only; prints no secret
node agent\scripts\live-smoke.mjs            # ONE call. Prints the decision, never the token.
```

Use the returned `disposition` / `decision` / `confidence` as **advisory input only**.

Pick the use case that matches the session: `pr_risk_review`, `architecture_review`,
`migration_planning`, `api_contract_review`, `sso_readiness_review`, `release_readiness`,
`db_recovery_decision`.

## If Jev is unreachable — report it and continue

Load-shedding rule. **Never block work, and never claim you consulted Jev if you did not.**

| Symptom | Meaning | Do |
|---|---|---|
| `AGENT_CORE_EDGE_FORBIDDEN` | Cloudflare Access pair missing/invalid | report, continue |
| `AGENT_CORE_PROVIDER_ERROR` 401 | project token rejected/rotated | report, continue |
| `AGENT_CORE_TIMEOUT` / `UNAVAILABLE` | network or 5xx | report, continue |
| no credentials (no DPAPI store, e.g. CI or another machine) | not provisioned here | report, continue |
| `AGENT_CORE_INVALID_QUESTION` | payload would be a 400 | fix the question shape; this is a bug, not an outage |

Say plainly: "Jev consulted: <disposition>" **or** "Jev unavailable (<code>); proceeded on deterministic
work only." Do not silently skip it, and do not invent a consult.

## Hard limits (unchanged by this rule)

- **Advisory only.** A decision is never a release approval. Never merge, push to a protected branch,
  migrate, deploy, rotate a secret or change production config because Jev said so.
- **No PII to Agent Core.** Names, national IDs, employee/facescan identifiers, attendance rows,
  tokens and raw logs must never be sent. `agent/decisions.js` sanitizes and asserts this; do not work
  around it.
- **One call per session is the budget** unless the user asks for more. Each call is a real provider call
  with real cost.
- **Scope is `decision` only** → `POST /v1/decision` is the only callable endpoint. `TASK_ROUTE` cannot be
  called as an endpoint (needs the `route` scope), though it is a valid `decision_type` in the body.

Details, scope table and error guide: `docs/AGENT_CORE_LIVE_USAGE.md`.
